{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Show help for all public functions - 2026-03-04\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 PS C:\\Users\\Administrator> Start-VcfEdgeAtScale -?\line
\line
NAME\line
    Start-VcfEdgeAtScale\line
\line
SYNOPSIS\line
    Automates end-to-end vSphere Supervisor edge deployment at scale in VMware Cloud Foundation 9.x.\line
\line
\line
SYNTAX\line
    Start-VcfEdgeAtScale [-AcceptBadCheckResults] [[-CleanUp] <String>] [-ComputeOnly]\line
    [[-DelayBeforeAddingNextHostSeconds] <Int32>] [[-EdgeSite] <String>] [-Force] [[-InfrastructureJson] <String>]\line
    [[-LogLevel] <String>] [[-RollbackOnFailure] <Nullable`1>] [[-SupervisorJson] <String>] [-ValidateOnly] [-Version]\line
    [<CommonParameters>]\line
\line
\line
DESCRIPTION\line
    Start-VcfEdgeAtScale orchestrates vSphere Supervisor cluster preparation and deployment in\line
    VMware Cloud Foundation (VCF) 9.x environments. The function handles the deployment workflow including:\line
\line
    - vCenter and ESX host connection\line
    - ESX Cluster creation and host add\line
    - Datastore creation and storage policy configuration.\line
    - Virtual Distributed Switch (VDS) setup and port group configuration\line
    - vSphere Supervisor Deployment\line
    - ArgoCD installation and configuration for GitOps workflows\line
\line
\line
RELATED LINKS\line
\line
REMARKS\line
    To see the examples, type: "Get-Help Start-VcfEdgeAtScale -Examples"\line
    For more information, type: "Get-Help Start-VcfEdgeAtScale -Detailed"\line
    For technical information, type: "Get-Help Start-VcfEdgeAtScale -Full"\line
\line
PS C:\\Users\\Administrator> show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp -?\line
\line
NAME\line
    Show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp\line
\line
SYNOPSIS\line
    Displays a reference table for configuring supervisor.json file.\line
\line
\line
SYNTAX\line
    Show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp [[-Filter] <String>] [[-Format] <String>] [[-WidthThreshold] <Int32>]\line
    [<CommonParameters>]\line
\line
\line
DESCRIPTION\line
    This helper function displays a reference table of configuration keys for the supervisor.json file,\line
    with Required (Yes/No/Conditional) and Notes for each key.\line
\line
\line
RELATED LINKS\line
\line
REMARKS\line
    To see the examples, type: "Get-Help Show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp -Examples"\line
    For more information, type: "Get-Help Show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp -Detailed"\line
    For technical information, type: "Get-Help Show-SupervisorJsonConfigurationHelp -Full"\line
\line
PS C:\\Users\\Administrator> Show-InfrastructureJsonConfigurationHelp -?\line
