\line
[INFO] ========================================================================================================================\line
[INFO] Infrastructure.json Configuration Reference\line
[INFO] ========================================================================================================================\line
\line
\line
\line
Key                                                    Required    Notes\line
---                                                    --------    -----\line
common.vCenterName                                     Yes         vCenter FQDN, 9.0 or later. Script needs HTTPS access.\line
common.vCenterUser                                     Yes         vCenter login (e.g. administrator@vsphere.local); SSO supported.\line
common.vSanWitnessVmName                               No          vSAN witness VM name or FQDN; used by vSAN-OSA/ESA.\line
common.esxUser                                         No          ESX login. Omit to use default root.\line
common.esxUniquePasswordPerHost                        No          Boolean. Default false when not defined (one password for all hosts). true = prompt per host.\line
common.nonInteractivePassword                          No          Boolean. When true, uses VCENTER_COMMON_PASSWORD / ESX_COMMON_PASSWORD env vars.\line
common.labEnvironment                                  No          Boolean. When true, some vSAN health checks are relaxed. With -Force, bypasses cleanup confirmation.\line
common.datacenterName                                  Yes         Existing vSphere datacenter; clusters are created under it.\line
common.clusterNamePrefix                               No          Prefix for cluster names. Omit for default cluster; format \{prefix\}-\{edgeSite\}.\line
common.datastoreNamePrefix                             No          Prefix for datastore names. Omit for default datastore; format \{prefix\}-\{edgeSite\}.\line
common.supervisorNamePrefix                            No          Prefix for supervisor names. Omit for default supervisor; format \{prefix\}-\{edgeSite\}.\line
common.vdsNamePrefix                                   No          Prefix for VDS names. Omit for default VDS; format \{prefix\}-\{edgeSite\}.\line
common.supervisorContentLibraryDatastore               No          When the key is present, datastore for supervisor content library (must already exist); script runs\line
                                                                   Initialize-SupervisorContentLibrary. When the key is omitted (removed) entirely, the content library workflow is skipped.\line
common.supervisorContentLibrarySubscriptionUrl         No          When supervisorContentLibraryDatastore key is present, subscription URL for the content library. If omitted, default is\line
                                                                   https://wp-content.vmware.com/supervisor/v1/latest/lib.json.\line
common.vLcmImageName                                   No          vLCM image name in vCenter Image Catalog; omit to choose at run time.\line
common.vSanvMotionVmKernelMtuValue                     No          Optional. When defined, overrides the default MTU (9000) for the VDS and for vMotion/vSAN VMkernel adapters only. Mgmt (vmk0) and\line
                                                                   vSAN Witness (vmk3) are always 1500. Must be 1500-9190 (numbers only; validated at JSON load). Use 1500 when the physical path does\line
                                                                   not support jumbo frames.\line
common.vmkernelMtu                                     No          Optional. Legacy. MTU (1500-9190) for VDS and vMotion/vSAN VMkernels when common.vSanvMotionVmKernelMtuValue is not set. Mgmt and\line
                                                                   vSAN Witness are always 1500.\line
common.nicList                                         Conditional Array of NICs for the VDS (e.g. [\{"name":"vmnic1"\},\{"name":"vmnic2"\}]). Number of uplinks = length of nicList. Required at common or\line
                                                                   per cluster (clusters[].nicList); cluster overrides common. Must have 2 or 4 NICs.\line
common.contextName                                     Yes         VCF context name used by VCF CLI for ArgoCD.\line
clusters                                               Yes         Array of cluster configurations. Each cluster is identified by edgeSite and contains ESX hosts, supervisor services, storage policy,\line
                                                                   and networking.\line
clusters[].edgeSite                                    Yes         Unique site ID; must match one tkgsSiteSpec[].edgeSite in supervisor.json.\line
clusters[].nicList                                     Conditional Optional override for this cluster. When present (2 or 4 NICs), overrides common.nicList. At least one of common.nicList or\line
                                                                   clusters[].nicList must be defined per cluster.\line
clusters[].esxHosts                                    Yes         Array of ESX FQDNs or IPs; script needs HTTPS access to each host.\line
clusters[].supervisorServices.argoCdOperatorYamlPath   Yes         Path to ArgoCD operator YAML (escape backslashes on Windows).\line
clusters[].supervisorServices.argoCdDeploymentYamlPath Yes         Path to ArgoCD instance YAML; namespace in file must match nameSpacePrefix.\line
clusters[].supervisorServices.nameSpacePrefix          No          ArgoCD namespace prefix. Omit for default argocd; script appends cluster MoRef for uniqueness.\line
clusters[].supervisorServices.vmClass                  No          Array of VM class names for ArgoCD namespace. Omit to assign all VM classes from vCenter.\line
clusters[].storagePolicy.storagePolicyTagCatalog       No          Tag catalog for storage policy. Omit for default \{storageType\}-Storage-TagCatalog.\line
clusters[].storagePolicy.storageType                   Yes         Storage type: VMFS, vSAN-ESA, or vSAN-OSA.\line
clusters[].storagePolicy.storagePolicyRule             No          The only valid value is Fully initialized. Do not change otherwise the script will error.\line
clusters[].networking.networkSegments                  Yes         Array of segments; names must match supervisor.json network references.\line
clusters[].networking.networkSegments[].name           Yes         Segment name; lower-case, RFC1123; must match supervisor.json.\line
clusters[].networking.networkSegments[].vlanId         Yes         VLAN ID (0-4095); unique within this cluster.\line
clusters[].networking.networkSegments[].gateway        Yes         Gateway in CIDR (e.g. 10.30.10.1/24); mapped into supervisor by segment name.\line
clusters[].networking.networkingVmKernelInterfaces     Conditional Required for vSAN-ESA and vSAN-OSA only (not VMFS). At least two entries: vMotion, vSAN (required). Optional third: vSAN Witness.\line
                                                                   When vSAN Witness is omitted, mgmt (vmk0) is tagged with vSAN witness traffic; when present, a dedicated witness VMkernel (vmk3) is\line
                                                                   created. Each entry: service, vlanId (0-4095), netmask (valid IPv4 netmask), ipList (exactly two unique IPv4s, one per host). Only\line
                                                                   the vSAN Witness entry requires gateway.\par}
